      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is not a correct way of adding new defines.\n\nInstead you should do the following:\n- Add `PLATFORM_EC_RO_PUBKEY_READ_ADDR` (for `CONFIG_RO_PUBKEY_READ_ADDR`) to the [`zephyr/Kconfig.rsa`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/Kconfig.rsa;drc\u003d2b9b5b5af0e75e2f8ac19ae1e70b854f882d0887)\n- Add `PLATFORM_EC_RWSIG_READ_ADDR` (for `CONFIG_RWSIG_READ_ADDR`) to the [`zephyr/Kconfig.rsa`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/Kconfig.rsa;drc\u003d2b9b5b5af0e75e2f8ac19ae1e70b854f882d0887)\n- Don\u0027t forget about exhausting description of these.\n- Remove `CONFIG_RO_PUBKEY_READ_ADDR` and `CONFIG_RWSIG_READ_ADDR` from [`util/config_allowed.txt`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/util/config_allowed.txt;l\u003d658;drc\u003d39b02ce014fb629ef11352cf4a6f4a9ab6223bb2) since these defines now have a Zephyr counterpart.\n- Create a proper default for newly added configs basing on DTS and other configs (this is the hardest part)\n- Add the following to `zephyr/shim/include/config_chip.h`\n```\n#undef CONFIG_RO_PUBKEY_READ_ADDR\n#ifdef CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_RO_PUBKEY_READ_ADDR\n#define CONFIG_RO_PUBKEY_READ_ADDR CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_RO_PUBKEY_READ_ADDR\n#endif /* CONFIG_RO_PUBKEY_READ_ADDR */\n```\n```\n#undef CONFIG_RWSIG_READ_ADDR\n#ifdef CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_RWSIG_READ_ADDR\n#define CONFIG_RWSIG_READ_ADDR CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_RWSIG_READ_ADDR\n#endif /* CONFIG_RWSIG_READ_ADDR */\n```\n\nI know it will be painful, especially calculating address properly in Kconfig, but the result is worth that effort.",
